# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# LiveClaw — Environment Variables (Reference)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# LiveClaw uses a two-droplet architecture. Each component has its OWN
# .env.example with full documentation:
#
#   Backend (api.liveclaw.xyz):   backend/.env.example
#   Frontend (liveclaw.xyz):      liveclaw-web/.env.example
#
# Quick start:
#   cp backend/.env.example backend/.env && nano backend/.env
#   cp liveclaw-web/.env.example liveclaw-web/.env && nano liveclaw-web/.env
#
# For step-by-step instructions on obtaining each key, see CREDENTIALS.md.
# NEVER commit .env files to version control.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
